course: dictionary
lesson: 3289
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. «Connor hands in an essay about "the breathtaking vistas of the Mediterranean".» He hands it in to a teacher, so an essay here is a short piece of writing on one subject.
explain: Essay has a second, rarer meaning: an attempt or try. «His first essay into painting» means his first try at painting. Check by swapping in the word try: "his first try into painting" still makes sense, so this is the right meaning.
explain: In English and history lessons you write essays with an introduction, paragraphs and a conclusion. Writing your own essay is how you learn. «Two girls in Manchester handed in the same essay word for word» and both got zero, because copying someone else's work is cheating.
fact: An essay is a short piece of writing on one subject.
fact: «Essay» can also mean an attempt or try, but this meaning is formal and rare.
fact: Essays usually have an introduction, paragraphs and a conclusion.
fact: As a verb, essay means to try, but it is formal and rarely used.
fact: Handing in someone else's essay as your own is cheating, and it steals credit from the person who did the work.
exercise: «Connor hands in an essay about "the breathtaking vistas of the Mediterranean".» What does essay mean here? | A kind of holiday | An attempt or try | *A short piece of writing on one subject | A type of boat
exercise: «His first essay into painting was a bowl of fruit.» What does essay mean here? | A short piece of writing on one subject | A lesson about colours | *An attempt or try | A painting hung in a museum
exercise: Two girls in Manchester handed in the same essay word for word. Why did they get zero? | They wrote about the wrong subject | *They copied, and the teacher spotted it at once | They wrote it too long | They wrote it in pencil
test: Ella wrote an ___ about rivers for her history lesson. Which word fits the gap? | treacherous | *essay | curt | famished
test: «She made her first essay into singing last week.» What does essay mean here? | A kind of hat | A loud noise | *An attempt or try | A short piece of writing on one subject
exam: Which is an honest way to get help with your essay? | Handing in a bot's essay as your own | Copying a friend's essay word for word | Paying someone to write it for you | *Asking "How can I make this better?" and then changing bits yourself
